From 4149a33ac0360be7f97834f19ee30217c00a7d9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Candice Cantrelle <glowstick.2017@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 02:26:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Resolve every path against the site's mount point, and repair
 the archive
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The rebuild addressed everything from the domain root. The repository is
owned by Unicorn0-0Cakes and named candicecantrelle.github.io, which makes
it a project site served under /candicecantrelle.github.io/ rather than a
user site, so all 304 root-relative references resolved one level above the
site and returned 404 — unstyled HTML with dead navigation.

Static references in the 40 HTML pages are now depth-correct relative paths.
shell.js works the base out from its own script URL and exposes it to
cards.js, so JavaScript-generated navigation, card links and registry image
paths resolve the same way. 404.html resolves its own base at parse time,
since a 404 is served at whatever depth was requested. Nothing is hardcoded
to the current host, so moving to a user site or a custom domain later needs
no further changes.

Separately, moving the old site into /archive/ had shifted every page one
level deeper without adjusting its references, so 101 of them pointed at
nothing — that was broken at the domain root too, not a side effect of the
subpath. Each is re-resolved against where its target actually lives now.
Also fixes a filename typo the old site shipped with (luxury-environment.png
against a file named luxury-enviroment.png).

Verified by crawling all 40 pages under a simulated project subpath with a
headless browser: every stylesheet, script, image and internal link returns
200. The five remaining 404s are archived pages referencing images that were
never committed to this repository, broken on the live site since 2024.
